     Yahtzee(6l)              OS9/68000 V2.1               Yahtzee(6l)     NAME          yahtzee - the game of yahtzee     SYNOPSIS          yyaahhttzzeeee [[--dd]] [[--NN]] [[--ss]] [[--hh]]     DESCRIPTION          _Y_a_h_t_z_e_e is a computer simulation of the game of the same          name.  This version of Yahtzee allows up to six players,          where players can be either users at the same terminal or a          computer simulation of a player.          Full on-line help is available at all times by pressing the          question mark character. If you are unfamiliar with the          rules a rule book is also available at all times by pressing          the 'b' key.          Options are:          --dd   don't use the standout mode of the terminal          --NN   play _y_a_h_t_z_e_e non-stop, good if all players are computer               simulations          --ss   display the high score file          --hh   give command line options          At the end of each game the player with the highest score is          eligible to have their score recorded in the high score          file.     BUGS          Unknown, but please send bug problems to          {utzoo,utcsri,lsuc}!hcr!stacey.     AUTHOR          Stacey Campbell - HCR Corporation, Toronto, Canada, 1988.     Page 1                                          (printed 6/28/88)